<section class="hero">
	<h1>Software engineering is changing shape.</h1>
	<p class="hero-lead">
		Writing code has never been cheaper. AI assistants can draft functions, tests and whole features in minutes, which moves the hard part of the job somewhere else: deciding what to build, how the pieces fit together, and how to keep it running when real users and real money are involved.
	</p>
	<p class="hero-lead">
		My bet is that the next few years reward engineers who can reason about systems, data and trade-offs, not just produce syntax. When generating code is easy, judgement, architecture and reliability become the scarce skills, and reviewing what gets built becomes the real bottleneck.
	</p>
	<p class="hero-lead">
		This site is where I think that through, in longer articles and shorter notes.
	</p>
	<p class="hero-actions">
		<a class="button" href="/blog/">Read the articles</a>
		<a class="button button-secondary" href="/about/">About me</a>
	</p>
</section>

